ube.com/watch?v=4y3B0tx7y_8). Before that, the Bank had held at 2.25% for seven meetings in a row, [per CBC](https://www.cbc.ca/news/business/livestory/bank-of-canada-interest-rate-announcement-oct-28-9.7398140).\n- **What's next:** The Bank said [more increases may be needed](https://www.bankofcanada.ca/2026/10/fad-press-release-2026-10-28) but it will \"proceed carefully\". [TD's commentary](https://stories.td.com/ca/en/article/bank-of-canada-interest-rate-october-2026) expects one more hike, to 2.75%, and then a more cautious approach.\n\nIf you meant a different bank, such as the Fed, the ECB, or your own bank's mortgage or savings rates, tell me which one and I'll look it up. I can also set up a watch that alerts you when a rate changes."}]},"stop_reason":"end_turn","usage":{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":664,"cache_read_input_tokens":4813,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3224},"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","refusal_category":null}]}
